<title>UK: BT Q2 pretax profit hit by charges.</title>
<headline>BT Q2 pretax profit hit by charges.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Second quarter to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		7.3		    vs 7.6</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 7.9		    vs 7.45</p>
<p> Pretax		     730		    vs 732</p>
<p> Turnover		   3.725 billion	vs 3.549 billion</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 670 to 681 million stg. Half year pretax profits, which came in at 1.599 billion stg against 1.606 billion last year, included a 60 million stg premium on the repurchase of bonds and a 235 million stg redundancy charge.  </p>
<p> Operating costs	  2.955 billion	vs 2.751 billion</p>
<p> Operating profit	 770		    vs 798</p>
<p> Redundancy charge (H2) 235		    vs 123</p>
<p> Bond repurchase premium60		     vs nil</p>
<p> Interest payable	 84		     vs 91</p>
<p> Tax			  261		    vs 249</p>
<p> Net taxed		  469		    vs 483</p>
<p> Attributable	     461		    vs 479</p>
<p> Pay date		   Feb 17, 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  Jan 8, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE - Operating costs included redundancy charges. BT, which announced it would merge with America's MCI on November 3, has announced an expected total dividend of 19.85p for the year to March 1997. This does not include a 35 pence per share special dividend, also announced alongside the MCI deal.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7987</p>
</text>
